10% of $2000 is $200, so Janeth needs to return $2000 + $200 = $2200. If she pays $165 a month for 12 months, she will pay a total of $165 * 12 = $1980. Her remaining balance will be $2200 - $1980 = $220.

So the answer is
\boxed{220}

Erin begins with 7 lollipops. Her mother gives her 10 more, so she has 7 + 10 = 17 lollipops.

Erin then gives 3 lollipops to Ella. Therefore, she has 17 - 3 = 14 lollipops left.

